:: Title_Screen [title] {"position":"300,100","size":"100,100"}
# The Shifting Spire
*Occult Time-Travel Thriller with Dark Comedy* • *Surreal tension laced with anachronistic irony, escalating from mundane corporate dread to cosmic horror*

> [!NOTE]
> **Content Advisory:** Mature 18+ (Explicit Uncensored Content)

**The Conflict:** The irreconcilable tension between preserving linear time and allowing its deliberate collapse for godlike power, embodied in Marcus’s desperate collection of artifact fragments while the cult pushes for merger and a single past alteration threatens to unravel the ritual’s solution in the present.

**Themes:** Reincarnation and the cyclical prison of history, Corporate power as eternal tyranny, Identity fractured across timelines, Unintended consequences of tampering with fate, Sanity versus the seductive pull of collapsed time

**Protagonist:** Marcus Hale, a skeptical junior real estate broker whose impulsive need to prove himself masks a deep moral wound: his last deal cost a colleague their career and livelihood. Thrust from mundane onboarding into accidental activation of an ancient device, he must navigate shifting eras while confronting whether he will repeat the same selfish patterns across centuries or break the cycle.

**Antagonist:** Harlan Voss, the immortal high priest of the cult and CEO of the organization. In every era he appears as the apex authority—modern CEO, medieval king, 1960s warden—driven by the belief that all souls are eternal property to be harvested when timelines merge. He views the protagonist as both pawn and key, leveraging Marcus’s accidental activation and lingering guilt to force participation in the final ritual or condemn reality to collapse.

### Emergent Character Traits
* **<span style='color:#E0A82E'>Cunning</span>**: The capacity to weaponize anachronisms, deceive reincarnated figures, and improvise temporal solutions through clever manipulation and quick thinking.
* **<span style='color:#2EA8E0'>Empathy</span>**: The ability to recognize and honor the timeless souls of coworkers across eras, forging bonds that reveal hidden ritual paths and force morally weighted choices.

