## Passage: Transition from Chapter 1 to Chapter 2

Marcus activates the brass elevator as the Iron Throne Hall warps around him, temporal currents yanking the space through layered realities. The car descends in a flicker of fluorescent-to-torchlight bleed, the medieval seal fragment on his lanyard glowing hot against his palm while distant boardroom murmurs and chain rattles echo from below. He steps out into the full vaulted hall where modern cubicle logic has fully surrendered to medieval hierarchy.

> "The elevator doors part onto braziers guttering across rushes where filing cabinets stand like sentries and courtiers in doublets mutter quarterly projections beneath the iron throne."

